    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "code": "root = [2, 1, 3]                     ->  true\nroot = [5, 1, 4, null, null, 3, 6]   ->  false   (4 is in 5's right subtree)\nroot = [5, 1, 6, null, null, 3, 7]   ->  false   (3 is in 5's right subtree)\nroot = [2, 2, 2]                     ->  false   (no duplicates: strictly less / greater)"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "The trap"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Checking only `left.val < node.val < right.val` at each node passes the tree above — and it's wrong. The rule is about **whole subtrees**. Two correct ways to enforce it: pass down the **range** each node must fit in, or check that the **in-order** walk is strictly increasing."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "1. Brute force: compare with every value below"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "At each node, check that the largest value in its left subtree is smaller and the smallest value in its right subtree is bigger — then check both subtrees the same way."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "javascript",
      "code": "function isValidBST(node) {\n  if (node === null) return true;\n  if (node.left !== null && max(node.left) >= node.val) return false;\n  if (node.right !== null && min(node.right) <= node.val) return false;\n  return isValidBST(node.left) && isValidBST(node.right);\n}\n\nfunction max(n) {                                // the largest value in this subtree\n  let m = n.val;\n  if (n.left !== null) m = Math.max(m, max(n.left));\n  if (n.right !== null) m = Math.max(m, max(n.right));\n  return m;\n}\n\nfunction min(n) {                                // the smallest value in this subtree\n  let m = n.val;\n  if (n.left !== null) m = Math.min(m, min(n.left));\n  if (n.right !== null) m = Math.min(m, min(n.right));\n  return m;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "code": "def is_valid_bst(node):\n    if node is None:\n        return True\n\n    def values(n):\n        return [] if n is None else [n.val] + values(n.left) + values(n.right)\n\n    left, right = values(node.left), values(node.right)\n    if left and max(left) >= node.val:\n        return False\n    if right and min(right) <= node.val:\n        return False\n    return is_valid_bst(node.left) and is_valid_bst(node.right)"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "java",
      "code": "boolean isValidBST(TreeNode node) {\n    if (node == null) return true;\n    if (node.left != null && max(node.left) >= node.val) return false;\n    if (node.right != null && min(node.right) <= node.val) return false;\n    return isValidBST(node.left) && isValidBST(node.right);\n}\n\nint max(TreeNode n) {\n    int m = n.val;\n    if (n.left != null) m = Math.max(m, max(n.left));\n    if (n.right != null) m = Math.max(m, max(n.right));\n    return m;\n}\n\nint min(TreeNode n) {\n    int m = n.val;\n    if (n.left != null) m = Math.min(m, min(n.left));\n    if (n.right != null) m = Math.min(m, min(n.right));\n    return m;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "code": "int maxOf(TreeNode* n) {\n    int m = n->val;\n    if (n->left) m = max(m, maxOf(n->left));\n    if (n->right) m = max(m, maxOf(n->right));\n    return m;\n}\n\nint minOf(TreeNode* n) {\n    int m = n->val;\n    if (n->left) m = min(m, minOf(n->left));\n    if (n->right) m = min(m, minOf(n->right));\n    return m;\n}\n\nbool isValidBST(TreeNode* node) {\n    if (node == nullptr) return true;\n    if (node->left && maxOf(node->left) >= node->val) return false;\n    if (node->right && minOf(node->right) <= node->val) return false;\n    return isValidBST(node->left) && isValidBST(node->right);\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Time O(n²)** in the worst case (every node scans its whole subtree), **space O(h).**"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "2. Pass down the allowed range"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "The root may be anything. Going **left** narrows the range from above (everything there must be below this node); going **right** narrows it from below. Each node just checks that it fits its range."
    },
    {
      "type": "simulator",
      "program": "validate-bst-range",
      "caption": "Each node carries the range its ancestors allow; one value outside it fails the tree."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "javascript",
      "code": "function isValidBST(root) {\n  const fits = (node, low, high) => {        // every value here must be strictly between low and high\n    if (node === null) return true;\n    if (node.val <= low || node.val >= high) return false;\n    return fits(node.left, low, node.val) && fits(node.right, node.val, high);\n  };\n  return fits(root, -Infinity, Infinity);\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "code": "def is_valid_bst(root):\n    def fits(node, low, high):            # every value here must be strictly between low and high\n        if node is None:\n            return True\n        if not low < node.val < high:\n            return False\n        return fits(node.left, low, node.val) and fits(node.right, node.val, high)\n\n    return fits(root, float(\"-inf\"), float(\"inf\"))"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "java",
      "code": "boolean isValidBST(TreeNode root) {\n    return fits(root, Long.MIN_VALUE, Long.MAX_VALUE);\n}\n\nboolean fits(TreeNode node, long low, long high) {   // strictly between low and high\n    if (node == null) return true;\n    if (node.val <= low || node.val >= high) return false;\n    return fits(node.left, low, node.val) && fits(node.right, node.val, high);\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "code": "bool fits(TreeNode* node, long long low, long long high) {   // strictly between low and high\n    if (node == nullptr) return true;\n    if (node->val <= low || node->val >= high) return false;\n    return fits(node->left, low, node->val) && fits(node->right, node->val, high);\n}\n\nbool isValidBST(TreeNode* root) {\n    return fits(root, LLONG_MIN, LLONG_MAX);\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Time O(n), space O(h).** Java and C++ use 64-bit bounds because a node may hold `Integer.MIN_VALUE` or `MAX_VALUE` itself."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "3. In-order must be strictly increasing"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "A binary tree is a BST exactly when its in-order walk is **strictly increasing**. Walk it and compare each value with the previous one."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "javascript",
      "code": "function isValidBST(root) {\n  let prev = null;\n  const inorder = (node) => {\n    if (node === null) return true;\n    if (!inorder(node.left)) return false;\n    if (prev !== null && node.val <= prev) return false;   // not bigger than the value before it\n    prev = node.val;\n    return inorder(node.right);\n  };\n  return inorder(root);\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "code": "def is_valid_bst(root):\n    prev = None\n\n    def inorder(node):\n        nonlocal prev\n        if node is None:\n            return True\n        if not inorder(node.left):\n            return False\n        if prev is not None and node.val <= prev:\n            return False                  # not bigger than the value before it\n        prev = node.val\n        return inorder(node.right)\n\n    return inorder(root)"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "java",
      "code": "Integer prev;\n\nboolean isValidBST(TreeNode root) {\n    prev = null;\n    return inorder(root);\n}\n\nboolean inorder(TreeNode node) {\n    if (node == null) return true;\n    if (!inorder(node.left)) return false;\n    if (prev != null && node.val <= prev) return false;   // not bigger than the value before it\n    prev = node.val;\n    return inorder(node.right);\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "code": "bool inorder(TreeNode* node, TreeNode*& prev) {\n    if (node == nullptr) return true;\n    if (!inorder(node->left, prev)) return false;\n    if (prev != nullptr && node->val <= prev->val) return false;   // not bigger than the value before it\n    prev = node;\n    return inorder(node->right, prev);\n}\n\nbool isValidBST(TreeNode* root) {\n    TreeNode* prev = nullptr;\n    return inorder(root, prev);\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Time O(n), space O(h).** It stops at the first value out of order."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Comparing the approaches"
    },
    {
      "type": "complexity",
      "rows": [
        {
          "approach": "Brute force: compare with every value below",
          "time": "O(n²)",
          "timeWhy": "Each node scans its **whole subtree**: up to **n²/2** checks on a chain.",
          "space": "O(h)",
          "spaceWhy": "Recursion **as deep as the tree**."
        },
        {
          "approach": "Pass down the allowed range",
          "time": "O(n)",
          "timeWhy": "Each node is checked **once** against its `(low, high)` bounds.",
          "space": "O(h)",
          "spaceWhy": "Recursion **as deep as the tree**."
        },
        {
          "approach": "In-order must be strictly increasing",
          "time": "O(n)",
          "timeWhy": "One in-order pass, **stopping** at the first value out of order.",
          "space": "O(h)",
          "spaceWhy": "The recursion, plus one **previous value**."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Edge cases to test"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "**Duplicates** — `[2, 2, 2]` is not a BST under the strict rule.",
        "**Extreme values** — `[2147483647]` must be valid: don't use int bounds as \"no limit\".",
        "**A grandchild out of range** — the trap above: `[5, 1, 6, null, null, 3, 7]`.",
        "**Empty tree** — valid."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Variations"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "**Recover Binary Search Tree** — exactly two values were swapped: find them with the same in-order check (Pattern 3).",
        "**Largest BST subtree / Maximum Sum BST** — validate every subtree bottom-up in one pass (Pattern 5).",
        "**Validate with duplicates allowed on one side** — make one comparison non-strict."
      ]
    }
  ],
